  "description": "XAYYEF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C148 H104 N20 O56 Yb4 Zn12,8(C3 H7 N1 O1),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 6 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn5 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn6 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Zn7 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn8 (Zn) has 6 O neighbors; Zn9 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn10 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn11 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn12 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Yb1A? (Yb) has 0 O neighbors; Yb1B? (Yb) has 0 O neighbors; Yb2A? (Yb) has 0 O neighbors; Yb2B? (Yb) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.260-4.572 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.35-129.95°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Yb4Zn12(quinHA)10(ph)2(Hph)4(OH)4(H2O)4·8H2O·4DMF. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II), I(I).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
